+            // on the entry widget's own CSS class — so `.foregroundColor(...)` was
+            // silently discarded. The entry also paints an opaque themed background
+            // over whatever `.background(...)` drew behind it. Together those render
+            // white dark-theme text on a light themed field: invisible. Inheriting the
+            // colour and dropping the entry's own background makes `.foregroundColor`
+            // and `.background` behave as written, in every widget state (an unstyled
